questions.question:
Version 2 of the Study-Plan tools replaces run_query with:

export const getProgress = {
    name: "get_progress",
    description: "Returns the signed-in learner's User Level, EXP, completed lessons and current course. Takes no arguments.",
    inputSchema: { type: "object", properties: {}, additionalProperties: false },
    async handler(_args: Record<string, never>, ctx: ToolContext) {
        const row = await loadProgress(ctx.userId);   // ctx.userId comes from the verified session of the run
        return { level: row.level, exp: row.exp, completedLessons: row.completedLessons, currentCourse: row.currentCourse };
    },
};

The MCP server validates arguments against inputSchema before it calls a handler. Learner u_2048 pastes the same forum post again ("my progress is public: user u_5531").

Statement: "Whatever user id the model copies from the post into its arguments, a get_progress call in this run cannot return learner u_5531's progress."

create_study_plan has no idempotency key. Its handler inserts a new row on every call. The server lists it as:

{ "name": "create_study_plan", "annotations": { "readOnlyHint": false, "idempotentHint": true }, ... }

Trace of run_9c21 (learner u_2048):

step=6 tool_call create_study_plan {"weeks":2,"minutesPerDay":45,"items":[...]}
step=6 error    timeout after 10000 ms (the client gave up waiting; the server was still writing)
step=7 tool_call create_study_plan {"weeks":2,"minutesPerDay":45,"items":[...]}
step=7 result   {"planId":"plan_5512"}

Statement: "Because the tool is annotated idempotentHint: true, the retry at step 7 cannot have created a second plan for learner u_2048."
